    "result_text": "Tests still green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Changes made\n\nI agreed with both findings \u2014 they're coherence cleanups, not logic objections \u2014 and addressed them:\n\n1. **Duplicated country-code literal** \u2014 `hasValidNationalLength` now reuses the existing `DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE` constant instead of a hardcoded `\"61\"`, so Australia's code lives in one place. The NANP code is likewise a named constant (`NANP_COUNTRY_CODE`).\n\n2. **Coupled magic numbers** \u2014 the `- 2` / `- 1` offsets are gone. A `nationalLength(e164Digits, countryCode)` helper derives the offset from `countryCode.length()`, so changing a country code can't leave a stale offset behind. The required national lengths are now named constants (`AU_NATIONAL_LENGTH = 9`, `NANP_NATIONAL_LENGTH = 10`) with doc comments tying each to its country code.\n\nThe behaviour is unchanged: `+61` still requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10, and any other country code falls through to the generic 8\u201315 digit bound. The acceptance test and full suite remain green.",
